Architectural Note on Unique Identifiers
Because many exchanges, agencies, and pipelines publish multiple variables inside a single HTML table, CSV file, or GRIB2 weather grid, the query string / fragment identifier (?point=... or #region=...) appended to each base URL above is what guarantees 100% uniqueness per agent. Each agent hits its assigned URL, parses only its designated cell/parameter, and writes a strict 4-column record (agent_id, target_timestamp, available_timestamp, value).
